WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.826
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:09.640
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:17.039
Unit eight: Articles and Prepositions. Today you will use a, an, the and prepositions of time and place correctly.

4
00:00:17.339 --> 00:00:19.957
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.028
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:25.815
Article.

7
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:28.572
Article means a, an or the.

8
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:30.335
A is an article.

9
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.475
Your turn. Say: Article.

10
00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:37.056
Article.

11
00:00:37.817 --> 00:00:38.911
Preposition.

12
00:00:39.917 --> 00:00:42.775
Preposition means a word like in, on or at.

13
00:00:43.383 --> 00:00:44.849
At is a preposition.

14
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.137
Your turn. Say: Preposition.

15
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.920
Preposition.

16
00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:53.406
In.

17
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:56.997
In means inside a place or a long period.

18
00:00:57.583 --> 00:00:58.886
In May, in the room.

19
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:01.660
Your turn. Say: In.

20
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.280
In.

21
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:06.739
On.

22
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.866
On means a day or a surface.

23
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.101
On Monday, on the table.

24
00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:14.812
Your turn. Say: On.

25
00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:18.285
On.

26
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:19.784
At.

27
00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:22.516
At means a time or a point.

28
00:01:23.117 --> 00:01:24.861
At six, at the station.

29
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.835
Your turn. Say: At.

30
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.295
At.

31
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:32.947
Between.

32
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.019
Between means in the middle of two things.

33
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:38.233
Between the bank and the shop.

34
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:40.958
Your turn. Say: Between.

35
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:44.871
Between.

36
00:01:45.617 --> 00:01:46.595
Next to.

37
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:49.153
Next to means beside.

38
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.192
Next to the school.

39
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:54.041
Your turn. Say: Next to.

40
00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:57.913
Next to.

41
00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.593
Opposite.

42
00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:02.177
Opposite means facing.

43
00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:04.144
Opposite the market.

44
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.251
Your turn. Say: Opposite.

45
00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:10.962
Opposite.

46
00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:15.429
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.283 --> 00:02:18.422
Visal, when do we use a, an and the?

48
00:02:19.517 --> 00:02:31.933
We use a before a consonant sound and an before a vowel sound, such as a book and an apple. We use the when the person or thing is known or unique, for example the sun.

49
00:02:33.017 --> 00:02:35.597
How do we use in, on and at for time?

50
00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:47.904
We use in for months, years and seasons, such as in May. We use on for days and dates, such as on Monday, and at for clock times, such as at six o'clock.

51
00:02:49.017 --> 00:02:50.204
And for place?

52
00:02:51.317 --> 00:03:05.974
We use in for areas, on for surfaces, and at for points: in Cambodia, on the table, at the bus stop. We also use next to, between and opposite to describe positions.

53
00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:08.599
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.912
Grammar focus: Time and place: in and on and at.

55
00:03:13.212 --> 00:03:14.283
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:17.412
The class starts at seven o'clock on Monday.

57
00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:20.804
The bank is between the school and the market.

58
00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:28.157
Use a before consonants, an before vowels and the for known things. Learn in, on and at for time and place.

59
00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:32.927
Be careful! Don't say: The class starts in seven o'clock.

60
00:03:34.867 --> 00:03:37.598
Say: The class starts at seven o'clock.

61
00:03:37.898 --> 00:03:39.607
Use at with clock times.

62
00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.145
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:44.992
Finding the Way.

64
00:03:45.292 --> 00:03:47.965
The school is on a quiet street in Siem Reap.

65
00:03:48.967 --> 00:03:51.802
It is opposite the market and next to a small bank.

66
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.101
Classes start at seven o'clock in the morning.

67
00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.831
On Saturday there is a football match at the stadium.

68
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:02.634
Visitors can park between the bank and the library.

69
00:04:03.733 --> 00:04:07.491
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.723
I have blank umbrella.

71
00:04:10.023 --> 00:04:12.422
A, a. B, the. C, an.

72
00:04:15.967 --> 00:04:17.804
The answer is C: an.

73
00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.182
The class starts blank seven o'clock.

74
00:04:21.482 --> 00:04:24.439
A, at. B, in. C, on.

75
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.558
The answer is A: at.

76
00:04:30.717 --> 00:04:32.461
My birthday is blank May.

77
00:04:32.761 --> 00:04:35.358
A, at. B, in. C, on.

78
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.435
The answer is B: in.

79
00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:43.827
The bank is blank the school and the market.

80
00:04:44.127 --> 00:04:46.805
A, at. B, on. C, between.

81
00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.645
The answer is C: between.

82
00:04:53.783 --> 00:04:55.086
Where is the school?

83
00:04:55.386 --> 00:04:59.446
A, opposite the market. B, on a mountain. C, at sea.

84
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.499
The answer is A: opposite the market.

85
00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.701
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.433
Describe where your school is.

87
00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.739
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:23.039 --> 00:05:33.623
My school is in a small town in Cambodia. It is next to a bank and opposite the market. Classes start at seven o'clock, and we have an English lesson on Monday.

89
00:05:33.923 --> 00:05:35.691
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:41.848
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and time and place: in and on and at.

91
00:05:42.148 --> 00:05:45.868
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

92
00:05:46.168 --> 00:05:48.426
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

93
00:05:48.726 --> 00:05:51.355
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

